## Summary
The Trump administration is reportedly preparing to revoke business and tourism visas of up to 200,000 people seeking asylum in the US, in what media describe as the largest visa revocation effort ever. The move targets asylum seekers who entered the country on temporary visitor visas.

## Key Points
- The Trump administration plans to revoke up to 200,000 visas held by asylum seekers
- The revocations would affect both business and tourism visas
- This is described by media as the largest visa revocation action in history
- The targets are individuals currently seeking asylum in the United States


